{
  "_readme": [
    "Human-reviewed facts about each demo clip in the client's library.",
    "",
    "Automatic detection of rep counts was tried three ways (frequency analysis,",
    "pose-distance peaks, subject tracking) and none of them was trustworthy on",
    "clips this short, so every entry here was checked by eye against the contact",
    "sheets in review_sheets/. analyze_clips.py reads reps_per_loop from this file",
    "and its own measurement loses.",
    "",
    "reps_per_loop is how many complete reps one play of the clip shows, which is",
    "what lets the player loop the clip the right number of times and count along.",
    "It is null for holds, which run on a plain countdown instead.",
    "",
    "If a count looks wrong in the app, fix it here and re-run the seed. Nothing",
    "else needs to change."
  ],
